**22\.5 hours/week**

CASS Care Ltd is a multi\-disciplined community services provider, with "CASS", as our brand name, which is commonly known in the community. We are active in the provision of a comprehensive range of social welfare services, catering for needs from cradle to seniors, including residential aged care, home ageing, disability, settlement and health, employment and training, child care and many more community\-based services. We are seeking an enthusiastic person with relevant skills to fill the above position.

**Position Summary:**

The Community Services Worker (Indonesian Speaking) will engage with and support the Indonesian community by identifying community needs and delivering appropriate programs, information sessions, activities and events. The role will also provide information and referral support to connect community members with appropriate services.

**Main Duties and Responsibilities:**

* Engage with the Indonesian community through outreach and networking to identify community needs and inform the development of appropriate programs and activities;
* Plan, organise, coordinate and deliver information sessions, community programs and events in response to identified community needs;
* Provide culturally appropriate information and guidance on social welfare systems and community support, and connect community members with appropriate services when required;
* Coordinate and support the delivery of community and social group activities;
* Prepare and publish social media content to promote CASS services, programs and events;
* Prepare and adapt culturally and linguistically appropriate resources to improve understanding of available services and support;
* Coordinate volunteers as required and collaborate with internal teams and external stakeholders to support effective service delivery; and
* Maintain appropriate program and service records and contribute to relevant reporting requirements.

**Selection Criteria:**

**Essential**

* Tertiary qualification recognised in Australia and relevant experience;
* Knowledge of social welfare systems, government and community services and networks;
* Excellent command of spoken and written English and fluency in Indonesian;
* Strong interpersonal, communication and networking skills in English and Indonesian, including the ability to engage effectively with community members, including seniors;
* Ability to plan, coordinate and deliver community programs, information sessions, group activities and events;
* Proficient in using computers;
* Strong attention to detail and ability to explain information clearly;
* Strong organisational and time\-management skills and ability to work independently and in a team, meet deadlines and fulfil program requirements;
* Ability to use social media to support community engagement and service promotion;
* Current First Aid Certificate or ability to obtain one before employment;
* Valid National Police Certificate or ability to obtain one before employment; and
* Valid driver's licence and access to vehicle covered by comprehensive car insurance.

**Desirable**

* Relevant knowledge and experience in the community services sector;
* Experience coordinating community programs, events or group activities; and
* Experience working with Indonesian\-speaking community members and/or culturally and linguistically diverse communities, including seniors.

Salary and employment conditions for the above position are as per the Enterprise Agreement. Salary packaging is available. Discounted childcare fees are available for CASS's long day care, before and after school, and vacation care services.

**How to Apply:**

Applications in writing providing detailed resume, responses to the above requirements are to be forwarded to: Ms. Vickie Xu, Senior Executive Officer/Operations Support, CASS Care Ltd, 44\-50 Sixth Avenue, Campsie NSW 2194 or via email to recruitment@cass.org.au. Applications close at **5:00 pm, Friday, 2 October 2026**.

For enquiries regarding the position, please contact Ms. Sarah Chang, Senior Executive Officer/Multicultural Community Services Development on 0411 572 267\.

Only shortlisted applicants for an interview will be notified.

Job Type: Part\-time

Pay: $43,700\.00 – $48,700\.00 per year

Language:

* Indonesian (Required)

Licence/Certification:

* Driver Licence (Preferred)
* First Aid Certification (Preferred)
* own vehicle (Preferred)
* National Police Certificate (Preferred)

Work Authorisation:

* Australia (Required)

Work Location: In person

**Indonesian Speaking**

CASS Care Ltd is a multi\-disciplined community services provider, with “CASS”, as our brand name, which is commonly known in the community. We are active in the provision of a comprehensive range of social welfare services, catering the needs from cradle to seniors, including residential aged care, home ageing, disability, settlement and health, employment and training, child care and many more community\-based services.

**Position Summary:** 

This position is responsible for supporting the effective delivery of Home Ageing Services (HAS) and ensuring day\-to\-day operations are carried out in accordance with government requirements, aged care service standards, and organisational policies and procedures.

**Main Duties and Responsibilities:** 

Arranging support for aged clients with **Indonesian\-speaking backgrounds** at home under the Support at Home Program and/or the Commonwealth Home Support Program (CHSP). This includes:

* Preparing assessments, care plans, client statements, service reports, and claims;
* Communicating with My Aged Care, support workers, and other stakeholders; engaging in networking and service promotion;
* Assisting in daily operations and providing general administrative support to the HAS Unit, including support to other team members, team leaders, and supervisors;
* Embedding the Statement of Rights, dignity of risk, and Aged Care Quality Standards into all care services;
* Confirming eligibility, completing onboarding tasks, delivering Support Plan Review processes, and maintaining accurate records;
* Monitoring budgets, Assistive Technology and Home Modifications pathways, Restorative Care Pathway and End of Life Pathway, ensuring compliance with program rules and claiming requirements; and
* Promoting wellness and reablement approaches, empowering clients to make informed decisions and maintain independence.

**Selection Criteria:**

**Essential**

* Tertiary qualification and/or experience in relevant field;
* Good command of spoken and written English;
* Must be able to speak and write Indonesian fluently;
* Good communication, interpersonal, time management, and organisational skills;
* Ability to pay attention to details;
* Computer literate;
* Ability to work as a team and independently;
* Current First Aid and National Police Certificates, or is able to obtain the certificates prior to employment;
* Valid driver’s licence and access to vehicle covered by comprehensive car insurance; and
* Have the right to work in aged care.

**Desirable** 

* Relevant qualifications (Certificate III/Certificate IV or Diploma in Community Services or Aged Care preferred);
* Relevant knowledge and experience in aged care services and Aged Care Quality Standards;
* Previous experience in aged care case management (Home Care Packages/CHSP); and
* Ability to speak other languages.

Salary and employment conditions for the above position is as per Enterprise Agreement. Salary packaging is available. Discount child care fees are available for CASS’s long day care, before and after school, and vacation care services.

**How to Apply:** 

Applications in writing providing detailed resume, responses to the above requirements are to be forwarded before **5:00pm, 25 September 2026** to Ms. Vickie Xu, Senior Executive Officer/Operations Support, CASS Care Ltd, 44\-50 Sixth Avenue, Campsie NSW 2194 or via email to recruitment@cass.org.au.

For enquiries on the position, please call Ms. Franslin Marwati, Executive Support Officer/Multicultural Home Ageing Services on 0434 534 260\.

Only shortlisted applicants for interview will be notified.

